23,2,,status,Ryuji,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
24,2,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a habit of losing ownership during crises and failing to adapt our scope to business changes.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Our hardware is outdated, and our peak season is a complete blackout for any system cutovers.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,May,,We have a history of skipping upgrades and dealing with messy data migrations from external teams.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are losing key administrators, and the depot supervisors tend to ignore standard training in favor of their own ways.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The board prefers operating expenses over capital, and fragmented licenses lead to creeping costs over time.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, if the peak season is that rigid, we need a vendor who can handle a very specific deployment window.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Exactly. And @May, if we keep skipping upgrades, a hosted solution might be safer than on-premise.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, does that mean we should avoid modular licenses if they tend to climb in price?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,I am worried about who will actually run this. We can't rely on external trainers alone.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, @May. A bundled or fixed-price model would be far more palatable to the board and my budget.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Misaki, that makes the ""ownership"" issue even worse. We need a single point of accountability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. A fragmented system will just fail in the yard.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,May,,"So we need something modern, integrated, and not reliant on a third-party migration team that leaves a mess.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"We need someone who stays on-site or provides very deep, lasting support for the crews.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Logic suggests a vendor with a fixed configuration and a clear, bundled cost structure.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we are all looking for stability and clear accountability.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,Stability in the yard and a realistic timeline.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,May,,And a system that doesn't just age into obsolescence.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Misaki,,And one that doesn't break the people left to manage it.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,We have a clear set of requirements for the candidates.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
