49,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
50,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Meridian seems safe with a regional team, but Anchor's on-site engineering is tempting for accountability.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Anchor is built for transport, but on-premise servers might lead to the upgrade issues May mentioned.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,May,,"Tessera's marketplace is too risky for ""aging in place,"" and Corvus is too modular.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Anchor's engineering team being present through rollout solves my concern about the supervisors and administrators.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Meridian's fixed configuration and hosted suite align perfectly with the board's spending patterns.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, would Meridian's regional team be enough to prevent the ""unowned"" outages I found?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Misaki, do you think Anchor's on-site presence outweighs the risk of us neglecting the servers?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,May,,I dislike the partner-led migration in Tessera. It sounds like the 2018 pay move disaster.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, yes. Having engineers here is the only way the depot supervisors will actually adopt the system.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Meridian's hosted model removes the server neglect risk entirely, Ryuji.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm leaning toward Anchor for the accountability, though Meridian is a close second.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I'll go with Anchor. The transport-specific build is vital for our yard devices.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,May,,I agree with Anchor. On-site engineers are better than a partner firm or a modular mess.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Misaki,,Anchor is my choice. We need that hands-on support for the staff.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While I prefer Meridian's financial profile, the consensus on operational survival is hard to ignore.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Midori,,It seems we have a winner.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,May,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Misaki,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall concede to the majority for the sake of harmony.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
